==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*flektō||}}, of {{unk|la|title=uncertain}} ultimate origin, lacking any solid Indo-European cognates. Possible {{der|la|ine-pro|-}} predecessors include {{m|ine-pro|*bʰleK-||}}, {{m|ine-pro|*dʰleK-||}}, and {{m|ine-pro|*gʷʰleK-||}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|flectō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|flectō|flex|flex}}

# I [[bend]], [[curve]] or [[bow]]
# I [[deviate]], [[distract]]
#: {{syn|la|arceō|prōpulsō|dēviō|dīvertō|dēclīnō|āvertō|āspernor|dēmoveō|dēflectō}}
# I [[turn]] or [[curl]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} I [[persuade]], [[prevail]] upon, or [[soften]]

